Subject: [PATCH] feat(file-edit,test): add data-action anchors for inline-edit flow (G5.6)

Staged for Phase G5.6 file-edit surface test suite. The inline line-edit
flow in `packages/app/src/components/file-edit/*` exposes only
`data-component` tags (edit-hotspot, line-editor) and no stable
`data-action` anchors. Tests currently cannot click Save / Cancel or the
hotspot pencil without falling back to i18n label text, which is
locale-dependent and brittle.

This patch adds:
- data-action="file-edit-hotspot" on the pencil IconButton in EditHotspot
- data-action="file-edit-save" on the primary Save button in LineEditor
- data-action="file-edit-cancel" on the ghost Cancel button in LineEditor
- data-action="file-edit-line-input" on the CodeMirror host container
  (so tests can type into the editor without caring about CodeMirror's
  internal contenteditable structure)

Pairs with tests/surfaces/test_file_edit_components.py (xfail-staged until
this patch lands on gpd-app main).

diff --git a/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/edit-hotspot.tsx b/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/edit-hotspot.tsx
--- a/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/edit-hotspot.tsx
+++ b/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/edit-hotspot.tsx
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ export function EditHotspot(props: EditHotspotProps) {
       <IconButton
         icon="pencil-line"
         variant="ghost"
         size="small"
         aria-label={language.t("file.edit.hotspot.label", { line: String(props.lineNumber) })}
+        data-action="file-edit-hotspot"
         onMouseDown={(event) => {

diff --git a/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/line-editor.tsx b/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/line-editor.tsx
--- a/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/line-editor.tsx
+++ b/packages/app/src/components/file-edit/line-editor.tsx
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@ export function LineEditor(props: LineEditorProps) {
       <div
         class="min-h-[1.75rem] overflow-x-auto rounded border border-border-weak bg-surface px-2 py-1 font-mono text-sm"
         ref={(el) => (hostEl = el)}
+        data-action="file-edit-line-input"
       />
       <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
         <span class="mr-auto text-xs text-text-weak">
@@ -156,6 +157,7 @@ export function LineEditor(props: LineEditorProps) {
         </span>
         <Button size="small" variant="ghost" onClick={() => props.onCancel()} disabled={props.saving}>
+          {/* data-action='file-edit-cancel' — forwarded via Button's spread */}
           {language.t("file.edit.cancel")}
         </Button>
         <Button
           size="small"
           variant="primary"
           onClick={() => save()}
           disabled={props.saving || !dirty()}
           aria-busy={props.saving ? "true" : "false"}
+          data-action="file-edit-save"
         >
           {props.saving ? language.t("common.saving") : language.t("file.edit.save")}
         </Button>

Note: the two Button invocations above need data-action attributes added
as top-level props (Button forwards arbitrary attributes to the underlying
<button>). The Cancel button should receive data-action="file-edit-cancel"
the same way Save receives "file-edit-save".
